…@lower-…@engine-…"},{"id":"spn-59477","text":" sealed + closes"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-36499","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-59478","text":"3. A real emitted episode — "},{"id":"spn-59479","marks":["code"],"text":"examples/eval-one/episodes/episode-<id>/"}]},{"id":"blk-36500","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59480","text":"A committed, five-signal 1.0 episode you can "},{"id":"spn-59481","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs verify-episode"},{"id":"spn-59482","text":" directly. Emitted by:"}]},{"id":"blk-36501","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ trvs eval-one examples/eval-one/residency-forge --output examples/eval-one/episodes \\\n      --platform linux-x86_64 -- python3 $PWD/test/fixtures/residency_agent.py\n  status ✓ ok · reward 1 · bundle …/episode-e125d77b…f415\n$ trvs verify-episode examples/eval-one/episodes/episode-e125d77b…f415\n  closure ✓ · artifacts ✓ · citations/patch/tests/identity/finding_completeness ✓\n  reward ✓ (1.0) · episode-id ✓ · verified ✓ closed"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36503","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59483","marks":["bold"],"text":"Note on the id:"},{"id":"spn-59484","text":" "},{"id":"spn-59485","marks":["code"],"text":"residency-forge"},{"id":"spn-59486","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-59487","marks":["code"],"text":"task_id"},{"id":"spn-59488","text":" bakes the acceptance command's absolute "},{"id":"spn-59489","marks":["code"],"text":"argv[0]"},{"id":"spn-59490","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-59491","marks":["code"],"text":"sys.executable"},{"id":"spn-59492","text":") — see the prior memo §6.3 — so the emitted "},{"id":"spn-59493","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-<id>"},{"id":"spn-59494","text":" is environment-specific and will differ on your machine. The "},{"id":"spn-59495","marks":["italic"],"text":"shape"},{"id":"spn-59496","text":" and closure are what to review; a fresh "},{"id":"spn-59497","marks":["code"],"text":"--output"},{"id":"spn-59498","text":" run on your box reproduces the same structure with your interpreter's path."}]}],"id":"blk-36502","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-36504","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-59499","text":"4. Reclassification you asked me to record"}]},{"id":"blk-36505","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59500","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-59501","marks":["code"],"text":"residency-forge"},{"id":"spn-59502","text":" bundle is a "},{"id":"spn-59503","marks":["bold"],"text":"five-signal conformance fixture"},{"id":"spn-59504","text":" — it exercises the full citations/patch/tests/identity contract deterministically via the stub agent. It is "},{"id":"spn-59505","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-59506","text":" a genuine Evidence Residency "},{"id":"spn-59507","marks":["italic"],"text":"finding"},{"id":"spn-59508","text":" about real code: the \"spec\" and \"src\" are minimal fixtures chosen to make each signal's pass/fail path reachable and byte-reproducible. Treat every reward/verdict in the examples + batteries as a "},{"id":"spn-59509","marks":["bold"],"text":"contract-conformance"},{"id":"spn-59510","text":" demonstration, not a substantive spec-vs-impl result. The first genuine spec/impl task (real repo, real finding) remains future work, gated behind TestPlanV2 + portable toolchain refs (below)."}]},{"id":"blk-36506","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-59511","text":"5. New autonomous decisions — please ratify or steer"}]},{"id":"blk-36507","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59512","text":"None move a content-addressed identity beyond Req 3 ("},{"id":"spn-59513","marks":["code"],"text":"verification_evidence"},{"id":"spn-59514","text":" into the allowlist) and Req 7 (the version-string widening) — both of which your ruling directed."}]},{"id":"blk-36508","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36510","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59515","marks":["bold"],"text":"Saved evidence files are re-checked against the receipt digest on verify."},{"id":"spn-59516","text":" The"}]}],"id":"blk-36509","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-36511","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59517","text":"ruling's replay check compares the "},{"id":"spn-59518","marks":["italic"],"text":"re-run"},{"id":"spn-59519","text":" verifier's digest to the receipt; I also added a check that the "},{"id":"spn-59520","marks":["bold"],"text":"persisted"},{"id":"spn-59521","text":" "},{"id":"spn-59522","marks":["code"],"text":"verifiers/<sig>.json"},{"id":"spn-59523","text":" bytes hash to the receipt digest, so tampering the kept file is caught even if the replay happens to reproduce the same state. (This is what "},{"id":"spn-59524","marks":["code"],"text":"tampered_verifier_evidence_file_rejected"},{"id":"spn-59525","text":" pins.) Say the word if you'd rather the saved file be treated as purely decorative."}]},{"id":"blk-36512","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36514","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59526","marks":["bold"],"text":"Runtime tamper (`policy_violations`) is not recomputed on replay."},{"id":"spn-59527","text":" A write-escape"}]}],"id":"blk-36513","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-36515","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59528","text":"is a "},{"id":"spn-59529","marks":["italic"],"text":"live-run observation"},{"id":"spn-59530","text":" not recoverable from a digest; replay scores the un-tampered path, and a saved receipt that lies about a tampered reward is caught by the episode-id self-consistency check ("},{"id":"spn-59531","marks":["code"],"text":"tampered_receipt_reward_rejected"},{"id":"spn-59532","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-36516","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36518","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59533","marks":["bold"],"text":"`--json` prints the receipt to stdout; the bundle path goes to stderr."},{"id":"spn-59534","text":" Keeps the"}]}],"id":"blk-36517","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-36519","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59535","text":"stdout contract (a pure episode receipt) byte-identical whether or not "},{"id":"spn-59536","marks":["code"],"text":"--output"},{"id":"spn-59537","text":" is set."}]},{"id":"blk-36520","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36522","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59538","text":"**"},{"id":"spn-59539","marks":["code"],"text":"verify-episode"},{"id":"spn-59540","text":" wires "},{"id":"spn-59541","marks":["code"],"text":"tests"},{"id":"spn-59542","text":" unconditionally and "},{"id":"spn-59543","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-59544","text":" when the engine is"}]}],"id":"blk-36521","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-36523","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59545","text":"locatable.** An engine-less box that verifies a bundle which scored "},{"id":"spn-59546","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-59547","text":" gets an honest signal "},{"id":"spn-59548","marks":["italic"],"text":"mismatch"},{"id":"spn-59549","text":" (never a false pass), plus a stderr warn."}]},{"id":"blk-36524","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36526","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59550","marks":["bold"],"text":"The manifest carries a non-canonical `created_at`."},{"id":"spn-59551","text":" Wall-clock provenance only;"}]}],"id":"blk-36525","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-36527","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59552","text":"it is outside every id and never read on verify."}]},{"id":"blk-36528","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-59553","text":"6. Future (NOT started — awaiting your steer)"}]},{"id":"blk-36529","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-59554","text":"In the order you set: "},{"id":"spn-59555","marks":["bold"],"text":"TestPlanV2 + portable toolchain refs"},{"id":"spn-59556","text":" → the "},{"id":"spn-59557","marks":["bold"],"text":"first genuine spec/impl task"},{"id":"spn-59558","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-59559","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs compare"},{"id":"spn-59560","text":